<title>USA: Anheuser-Busch Cos issues debt.</title>
<headline>Anheuser-Busch Cos issues debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt deal from Anheuser-Busch Cos Inc was issued on Monday, according to lead manager Dillion Read &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>Anheuser-Busch, headquartered in St. Louis, is the world's largest brewer and holds a 45-percent share of the U.S. beer market.</p>
<p>BORROWER ANHEUSER-BUSCH COS INC</p>
<p>AMT $250 MLN	 COUPON 7.125 PCT  MATURITY 7/1/2017</p>
<p>TYPE DEBENTURES    ISS PRICE 98.927  FIRST PAY DATE 1/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 7.227 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD 63 BPS     CALLABLE NON-CALL TEN</p>
</text>
